==Battleground==
*5 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 6~12 seconds<sup>180f~360f</sup>.
*1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*2 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s (800%) spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**4 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**10 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
**3 [[Dark Cyclone]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The Dark Cyclones are left trivially easy due to the existence of plenty of crowd-controllers and their high knockback counts causing them to be juggled easily. The problems are the Shadow Boxer Ks and burrowing [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], because the former shreds the frontline, the latter burrows into the middle of your backliner stack, and both are very good at destroying your crowd-control stack. If your crowd-control stack is destroyed, the Dark Cyclones will push especially hard due to their signature trait of insane DPS, their 20% knockback and fast speed for a Cyclone, not to mention there are 3 of them. There is also a rather rough start with Shadow Boxer Ks spawning in immediately with little time to prepare. Luckily, the stage has the Dark Cyclones spawn on base hit so it's possible to stack units such as [[Sanzo Cat]], [[Rodeo Cat]], and [[Bombercat]], if you happen to have any.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] - An easily stackable anti-[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] crowd-controller that shuts down the Cyclones. Note that its other forms (Bishop and Monk) are very bad overall because of their [[Single Attack]], so it is recommendable to not bring this cat unless it is in True Form.
*[[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] - Similarly to Sanzo, Rodeo Cat is a great, stackable crowd-controller, but it has [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] targeting which is especially helpful because it not only [[Slow|slows]] the cyclones, but also the SBKs.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] - While this Cat is really only usable in its True Form, it is easy to obtain and [[Freeze|freezes]] Dark enemies, with just two of them easily perma-freezing any Dark enemies it outranges, like the cyclones.
*[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] - One of, if not the best anti-[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] meatshield, which can also dish out decent DPS against them.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - A great, reliable anti-[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] that can defeat the SBKs rather quickly if protected, and also chip down the Cyclones if the [[Wave Attack|Wave]] Talent has been unlocked.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Jizo's Moving Castle|Kasa Jizo]] - Overall an amazing anti-Dark Uber that can deal with the SBKs while also being quite cheap.
*[[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Aethur Ltd.]] - Very good anti-Zombie Uber that at level 30 alone does over SIXTY THOUSAND damage to zombies in a single hit. That with its massive [[Omni Strike]] sniping results in most zombies in the level getting heavily crippled if not killed in one hit. In True Form, it also gains a very good 30% [[Dodge Attack|dodge]] chance and a guaranteed [[Survive|survive]], but having it is not needed.
*[[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Bomburr]] - Just like most of the other [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] ubers, Mighty Bomburr is a great anti-Zombie. He has a guaranteed chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] them, as well as great area damage (and of course also [[Zombie Killer]]).
*[[Seashore Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Seashore Kai]] - Has high health with a [[Special Abilities#Resist|resistance]] to [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Darks]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|zombies]] with [[Zombie Killer|Z-Kill]] and high damage, albeit at point-blank range. Seashore Kai is basically tailor-made for this stage.

